WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.750
Worlds that survive kill nine.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:10.300
A world is a project with its own state, budget, and lifecycle. Worlds nest inside worlds.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.575
Every change lands in an event log first. Nothing mutates without a record.

00:00:17.775 --> 00:00:22.575
Snapshots pin the ledger. Delegation never manufactures resources.

00:00:23.775 --> 00:00:30.025
Then the kill. Minus nine. No handler, no cleanup.  The process just dies.

00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:37.850
Reopen. The ledger prefix is intact, artifacts byte-identical, zero invokes re-executed.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:44.300
Worlds fuse and split with lineage: every merge records its parents.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.775
Exported composites run unmodified in a fresh directory.

00:00:50.975 --> 00:00:56.900
Limits, on the record: alpha, no learning, one host, crash only. No disk-loss magic.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.475
Worlds that survive kill nine.  Install the alpha.
